meta {
  name: 04 - Rejects a stale timestamp
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
  x-test-backdate-seconds: 400
}

body:json {
  {"type":1}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
}

docs {
  A genuinely valid signature over a timestamp outside the replay window, which
  `signature.ts` caps at ±300 seconds. The backdating is driven by the
  x-test-backdate-seconds header, which the collection script reads; the
  responder ignores headers it does not know.
  
  This is the difference between "signed by Discord" and "signed by Discord
  just now". Without the window a captured request replays forever, and every
  replay is a real model call on the bill.
  
  Needs testPrivateKeyHex set — unsigned, it would 401 for the wrong reason.
  Change the header to 60 and it should return 200 instead.
}
